course: dictionary
lesson: 11218
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The best way to choose the right one is to read the words around it. «The woodcutter swung his axe and the tree fell with a crash.» Swinging an axe at a tree tells you the woodcutter is a worker who chops down trees.
explain: Now read this: «The woodcutter's print of a bird hung in the gallery.» Print and gallery are the clues here, not axe or tree. In art, a woodcutter is a person who makes woodcuts, pictures printed from carved wood, so the word means something different this time.
explain: Fairy tales are full of woodcutters. In «Hansel and Gretel» and «Little Red Riding Hood», the woodcutter is a poor or brave forest worker. In Aesop's fable, «the honest woodcutter said only the iron axe was his», and fables are invented stories with a lesson.
fact: Woodcutter is a noun, and its plural is woodcutters.
fact: «Woodcutter» means a person whose job is cutting down trees or chopping wood.
fact: In art, «woodcutter» means a person who makes woodcuts, pictures printed from carved wood.
fact: Today the job of cutting down trees is usually called a forester or a logger.
fact: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
exercise: «The woodcutter swung his axe and the tree fell with a crash.» What does woodcutter mean here? | A tree that has been cut down | A person who makes pictures printed from carved wood | *A person whose job is chopping down trees | A bird that lives in the forest
exercise: «The woodcutter's print of a bird hung in the gallery.» Which meaning fits? | *A person who makes woodcuts, pictures printed from carved wood | A person whose job is chopping down trees | A person who keeps birds in a cage
exercise: Which clue tells you the woodcutter in «Hansel and Gretel» is a forest worker? | The children sleep in a palace | The story is set in a big town | *The woodcutter works among the trees in the forest
test: In «Little Red Riding Hood», what kind of worker is the woodcutter? | *A poor or brave forest worker | A painter who sells pictures | A king who rules the land | A teacher at a school
test: Which words are the clues that show the art meaning in «The woodcutter's print of a bird hung in the gallery»? | Tree and crash | Hungry and cold | *Print and gallery | Forest and axe
exam: What is the best way to choose between the two meanings of woodcutter? | *Read the words around it and check your meaning fits the sentence | Skip the sentence altogether | Always pick the job meaning | Ask a friend to guess for you
